('signals', 'SQ-0002', '{"area": "Strategy and projects", "at": "2026-10-22T08:00:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-22", "check": "Open the Department of Energy release. Confirm how much of the Dh250 billion is network spend and what connection volumes AI sites will request.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-22", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Network planning and engineering", "horizon": "Long", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Khaleej Times (published 12 Oct 2026): Dh250 billion, 60% clean target, 2 GW and 5 GW all confirmed; speaker is a named Department of Energy undersecretary at KEZAD Connect 2026. Caveats: 2 GW and 5 GW are power requirements, not spend; no grid or distribution breakdown. Evidence for ER-08 demand growth only.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-12", "risk_id": "ER-08", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "Abu Dhabi Department of Energy outlines a Dh250 billion energy and water investment for 2025 to 2035, targeting 60% clean electricity; AI infrastructure is put at about 2 GW in the first phase and 5 GW in the second.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://www.khaleejtimes.com/business/abu-dhabi-plans-dh250-billion-energy-investment-as-ai-demand-drives-power-needs"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0003', '{"area": "Cyber", "at": "2026-10-22T08:00:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-22", "check": "Confirm with the Cyber Security Council or WAM. Ask IT and OT security whether the organisation saw related attempts.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-22", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "IT and OT security", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (22 Sep 2026, updated 24 Sep): 640,000 attacks in a day and the April peak confirmed; Council head quoted naming Iran as one of the main players; energy, electricity and water named. Government agencies are attacked most; aviation comes from a separate Council statement. Still ask IT and OT security whether the organisation saw related attempts.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-09-22", "risk_id": "ER-03", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "The UAE recorded 640,000 cyberattacks in one day, below the April peak of nearly 800,000; the Cyber Security Council head calls Iran \"one of the main players\" and lists energy, electricity and water among the targets; government agencies are attacked most often.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/uae/2026/09/22/uae-companies-urged-to-remain-vigilant-on-cyber-attacks/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0004', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-22T08:00:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-22", "check": "Cross-check with UKMTO advisories. Ask Procurement whether open orders for transformers, cables or meters route via Hormuz or the Red Sea.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-22", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened gCaptain/Bloomberg (5 Oct 2026): all three facts confirmed. The 4 October tanker hit is a UKMTO report, not verified: cross-check UKMTO advisories. Ask Procurement whether open orders route via Hormuz or the Red Sea.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-05", "risk_id": "ER-01", "source": "gCaptain: shipping and Hormuz reporting", "summary": "LNG shipments through Hormuz rebounded in September but stay more than 75% below pre-war levels; a tanker was reported hit by an unknown projectile on 4 October; a September supply crunch pushed European and Asian prices to their highest since late 2022.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://gcaptain.com/lng-trade-through-hormuz-extends-rebound-despite-shipping-risks/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0005', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-22T08:00:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-22", "check": "US figures only. Ask Procurement for the organisation''s current transformer and switchgear lead times and supplier backlogs before accepting.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-22", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened pv magazine USA (11 May 2026): figures confirmed but US-focused; the 80% price rise is attributed to industry experts, not PwC; no mention of the Gulf. Exposure not shown, so Watch. It becomes a new risk (ER-12) if Procurement confirms the organisation''s lead times and backlogs are lengthening.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-05-11", "risk_id": "", "source": "pv magazine USA", "summary": "In the US market, lead times for high-capacity transformers reach up to four years (PwC) and prices are up roughly 80% over five years (industry experts); demand for generator step-up transformers rose 274% from 2019 to 2025 (Wood Mackenzie).", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://pv-magazine-usa.com/2026/05/11/u-s-transformer-market-faces-severe-supply-constraints-as-lead-times-extend-to-four-years/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0006', '{"area": "Legal and regulatory", "at": "2026-10-22T10:09:31.363Z", "by": "analyst", "captured": "2026-10-22", "check": "The page shows no date (January 2026 is inferred). Confirm date and status with the Department of Energy, and whether the tariff touches distribution charges.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "analyst", "decided_on": "2026-10-22", "decision": "New risk", "func": "Legal, regulatory and compliance", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened AGBI: the plan for a dedicated data-centre tariff is confirmed with a named Department of Energy source, but the page shows no date (January 2026 inferred) and does not say whether the tariff touches distribution charges. Watch until the Department of Energy confirms status and scope.", "proposed": false, "published": "2026-01", "risk_id": "ER-12", "source": "AGBI (Arabian Gulf Business Insight)", "summary": "Abu Dhabi''s Department of Energy plans a separate electricity tariff for data centres; suppliers will need to invest in more generation and grid infrastructure, the stated aim is to shield other customers from higher bills, though costs could still rise.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.agbi.com/energy/2026/01/abu-dhabi-plans-dedicated-power-tariff-for-ai-data-centres/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0007', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-23T04:45:57.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Cross-check the count against UKMTO: Gulf News (14 Oct) cites six Iranian attacks on 11 October. Ask Procurement whether open orders for transformers, cables or meters route via Hormuz.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Seatrade (13 Oct) and Gulf News (14 Oct). Both confirm attacks on vessels at Hormuz on or around 11 October, but the counts differ (four vs six). The Tasnim claim about the ADNOC tanker is unverified.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-13", "risk_id": "ER-01", "source": "Seatrade Maritime: security coverage", "summary": "UKMTO issued four reports of vessels struck by unknown projectiles at the Strait of Hormuz around 11 October: a container ship inbound, a crude tanker and a product tanker outbound, and a third tanker with its crew safe. Iran-affiliated Tasnim says the fire-damaged ADNOC VLCC Al Maqam transited without Iran''s authorisation; ADNOC has not commented and it is unclear whether it was one of the four reports.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://seatrade-maritime.com/security/ukmto-issues-four-hormuz-attack-reports-iran-claims-adnoc-tanker-strike"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0008', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-23T04:45:57.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Find a primary source (ADNOC, Fujairah authorities, UAE Ministry of Defence or NCEMA). Ask EWEC or Operations whether fuel or gas supply to power stations is affected.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system: Watch. Opened Gulf News (14 Oct). It is one secondary explainer, so it is not enough to add evidence to ER-02. Move to Add to existing risk ER-02 if a primary source confirms.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-14", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "Gulf News'' 14 October explainer reports drone or missile activity near Fujairah with temporary disruption to some loading and bunkering, and says Iran has threatened the ship-to-ship oil transfer system. It does not address power or water infrastructure; residents are told to follow NCEMA and Ministry of Defence channels.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/uae/us-iran-war-what-uae-residents-need-to-know-today-oct-14-2026-1.500709626"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0009', '{"area": "Finance", "at": "2026-10-23T04:45:57.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Confirm the market odds and inflation figures against the Fed and CME FedWatch before quoting them. Ask Finance and treasury how much floating-rate debt or planned issuance the organisation has.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Finance and treasury", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the CBUAE release (16 Sep 2026): base rate 3.9%, effective 17 Sep. The FOMC date (27-28 Oct, decision 28 Oct) is from fedratecalc.com. The hike odds and CPI figures come from a secondary article (political.org, 12 Oct) and are not verified. The CBUAE decision is older than the other signals but is new to the register.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-09-16", "risk_id": "ER-06", "source": "Central Bank of the UAE (CBUAE): base rate decisions", "summary": "The CBUAE raised its base rate by 25 basis points to 3.90% (from 3.65%), effective 17 September, after the Fed raised the interest rate on reserve balances by 25 bp. The Fed decides again on 28 October (22:00 Abu Dhabi time); a 12 October article put the chance of an October hike at about 16-18% and of a hike by year-end at 75-85%, with US inflation at 3.4% in August and 3.6-3.7% forecast for September on energy costs.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://centralbank.ae/media/dv3bo3ed/cbuae-raises-the-base-rate-by-25-basis-points-en.pdf"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0010', '{"area": "HSE", "at": "2026-10-23T04:45:57.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Ask Network operations whether rain caused faults, flooding at substations or manholes, or call spikes in Al Ain and Abu Dhabi this week. Check the NCM bulletin directly.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system: Watch. Opened The National (19 Oct) and Khaleej Times (16 and 20 Oct). No utility impact was reported, so this is context for ER-10 (Extreme heat and weather) rather than evidence. Add to ER-10 only if rain-related faults are confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-19", "risk_id": "", "source": "National Center of Meteorology (NCM)", "summary": "Heavy rain, hail and strong-wind alerts hit parts of the UAE between 16 and 20 October, and Al Ain roads were waterlogged on 16 October. The NCM''s five-day bulletin (19 October) forecasts more rain, wind and cloud until Friday 23 October, with heavy rain in Al Ain, Ras Al Khaimah and Fujairah until Wednesday. The articles report no power or road disruption.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/uae/2026/10/19/parts-of-uae-hit-by-heavy-rain-and-hail-as-alert-issued-over-50kph-winds/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0011', '{"area": "Legal and regulatory", "at": "2026-10-23T04:45:57.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Verify against the OFAC press release and the SDN list. Screen the organisation''s suppliers, shippers and contractors for the three UAE names.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Legal, regulatory and compliance", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system: Watch. Opened the Youverify digest (9 Oct). It is an aggregator and its own counts differ (55 vs 56 designations). I could not find the OFAC release, so the facts are not primary-sourced. If OFAC confirms and screening finds exposure, add to ER-05.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-09", "risk_id": "", "source": "Youverify Sanctions Monitor (aggregator)", "summary": "A sanctions digest dated 9 October lists US Iran-related designations of 8 October: 17 shipping companies and 17 tankers, plus 21 parties including UAE petrochemical traders. UAE-based names include Horizon Ship Management FZE (Ajman), Hessonite Ship Management LLC (Dubai) and Arabianpro Materials FZCO (Dubai). A general licence lets a Mumbai broker wind down until 23 October 2026.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://youverify.co/en/sanctions/2026-10-09"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0012', '{"area": "Strategy and projects", "at": "2026-10-23T04:45:57.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Ask Finance and treasury and Legal whether delisting changes bond covenants, disclosure duties or the information available through the ADX source. Check the ADX disclosure for the delisting date.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Finance and treasury", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system: Watch. Opened Khaleej Times (27 Aug). This is older than the other signals and was missing from the register. Decide whether it is a risk for the organisation or only context.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-08-27", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "TAQA''s board resolved on 25 August to delist the company and all its shares from the Abu Dhabi Securities Exchange after Abu Dhabi Power Corporation (ADPC) completed a squeeze-out and became the sole shareholder with 100% of issued share capital. Delisting takes effect once UAE regulatory approvals are received; the article gives no date and does not address bonds, financing or governance.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.khaleejtimes.com/business/taqa-to-delist-from-abu-dhabi-bourse-after-adpc-completes-100-takeover"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0013', '{"area": "Cyber", "at": "2026-10-23T05:57:43.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Ask the Cyber Security Council or aeCERT for the period covered and whether utilities or OT/SCADA were among the energy targets; compare with the organisation''s SOC alert volumes this month.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "IT and OT security", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the WAM report on Emirates 24|7 (21 Oct); only headline and summary were available. Unverified: period, whether OT or utilities were targeted, attribution. Follows SQ-0003 (640,000 in one day, 22 Sep).", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-21", "risk_id": "ER-03", "source": "WAM (Emirates News Agency): energy, cyber and government", "summary": "The UAE Cyber Security Council said national systems detected and blocked nearly 750,000 cyberattack attempts, with energy and education named as the top targeted sectors. Attack types cited: AI-powered attacks, phishing, DDoS and remote code execution attempts. The period covered is not stated.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.emirates247.com/uae/uae-blocked-750000-cyberattack-attempts-energy-and-education-sectors-were-the-top-targets/6964"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0014', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-23T05:57:43.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Check the UKMTO advisories page for both incidents and any change in JWC listed areas or war-risk rates; ask logistics whether inbound transformer, cable or meter shipments are affected.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Splash247 (22 Oct). UKMTO primary notices not opened. IRGC claims are unverified and recorded as claims only. Continues SQ-0004 and SQ-0007; new incidents.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-22", "risk_id": "ER-01", "source": "Splash247", "summary": "UKMTO warned of a tanker hit by a projectile 11 nm west of Bukha, Oman on 21 Oct (fire out, crew safe) and another 30 nm SE of Al Faw, Iraq on 20 Oct. The IRGC claimed seven vessels attacked or mined in the Gulf in 24 hours, without evidence; the US disputes the mine claims. IMO counts 119 confirmed incidents and 24 seafarer deaths since hostilities began.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://splash247.com/iran-claims-seven-vessels-hit-in-new-wave-of-hormuz-attacks"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0015', '{"area": "Finance", "at": "2026-10-23T05:57:43.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Ask Group Treasury how proceeds and pricing feed into the organisation''s funding cost and whether the AED 40 bn T&D allocation changes the organisation''s capex budget.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Finance and treasury", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened EnterpriseAM (21 Oct). Not verified against a TAQA press release or LSE listing. Strong demand and tight pricing may ease ER-06; coupons near 6% show the rate level. Related to SQ-0012 (delisting).", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-21", "risk_id": "ER-06", "source": "EnterpriseAM", "summary": "TAQA raised USD 1.75 bn on 20 Oct: a USD 1.1 bn 5-year green tranche at 5.875% (T+98 bps) and a USD 650 mn 10-year at 6.125% (T+108 bps), orders above USD 5.7 bn. First issue since going private. TAQA''s AED 75 bn capex plan to 2030 includes AED 40 bn for transmission and distribution.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://enterpriseam.com/uae/2026/10/21/taqa-raises-usd-1-75-bn-as-it-works-toward-aed-75-bn-in-capex-by-2030/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0016', '{"area": "HSE", "at": "2026-10-23T05:57:43.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Check NCM alerts for further convective events this week and ask control room for any weather-related faults or trips on 21 to 22 Oct.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Gulf News (updated 20 Oct), a grade C source; NCM primary alert not opened. Continues the unstable spell in SQ-0010 (16 to 20 Oct); may belong with ER-10.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-20", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "The Ministry of Interior issued a weather warning, using an NCM forecast, for rain, thunder, lightning and hail across parts of the UAE on 21 Oct, spreading from eastern to interior and western areas, with winds at times up to 50 km/h and light fog into 22 Oct. Highs of 38 to 40 C. Residents told to avoid wadis.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/uae/weather/uae-weather-alert-ministry-warns-of-hail-rain-and-thunderstorms-urges-caution-1.500717432"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0017', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-23T05:57:43.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-23", "check": "Ask Procurement whether cable and transformer contracts have copper price adjustment clauses and whether to time purchases on this dip.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-23", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened MINING.COM carrying Reuters (22 Oct). Not checked on LME directly. ER-07 (critical minerals) is closed, so not linked; prices remain near record levels.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-22", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "LME three-month copper fell 1.8% to USD 14,089/t on 22 Oct, a low of USD 14,031 being the weakest since 15 Sep. LME stocks rose to 272,950 t, highest since 24 Jul, as metal flowed back from COMEX. Cash traded at a USD 116 premium, showing near-term tightness. Aluminium and other base metals also fell.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.mining.com/web/copper-price-falls-to-five-week-low-as-lme-inventory-build-continues"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0018', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-24T04:40:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-24", "check": "Ask Procurement whether any transformer, cable or meter shipments are routed via Hormuz this quarter, and whether carriers have added surcharges or delays.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-24", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the Reuters story republished on BOE Report (23 Oct). Not checked against UKMTO or IMO pages directly. Article gives no war-risk premium or transit figures. Distinct from SQ-0014, which covers individual incidents.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-23", "risk_id": "ER-01", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "October is the worst month on record for attacks on shipping in and near Hormuz: 28 attacks per the Washington Institute (113 since 28 Feb). Over 30 VLCCs damaged, 11 in October. Marisks: 12 ships attacked 5-11 Oct, the highest weekly count. UKMTO logged 135 conflict-linked incidents by 16 Oct and a sharp rise in ship damage. Freight rates above USD 1 mn/day are drawing more tankers to load in the Gulf.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://boereport.com/2026/10/23/ship-attacks-in-strait-of-hormuz-hit-record-high-in-october/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0019', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-24T04:40:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-24", "check": "Ask Network operations whether lessons from the May loss of off-site power (grid restoration, load shedding) have been reflected in distribution contingency plans.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-24", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (20 Oct, updated 21 Oct). The strike itself was in May and is not otherwise in the signal list; this is the IAEA mission outcome. Not checked on IAEA or FANR sites. Article does not say how the grid or distribution was affected.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-20", "risk_id": "ER-02", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "An IAEA team (12-20 Oct, at UAE request) concluded that UAE authorities and Barakah responded appropriately to the 17 May drone strike, launched from Iraq, which hit a generator outside the inner perimeter, caused a fire and a loss of off-site power. The IAEA urged continued implementation of lessons learned. FANR said the UAE will keep working to protect nuclear facilities.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/uae/2026/10/20/nuclear-watchdog-praises-uae-response-to-drone-strike-on-barakah-plant/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0020', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-24T04:40:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-24", "check": "Check with HSE and Security whether contractor safety and drone-alert procedures for remote Abu Dhabi substations near the western border are current.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-24", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "HSE", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (21 Oct, updated 22 Oct). Gulf News (23 Oct) also reports it and says Aramco told essential eastern HQ staff to work from home. Shaybah''s distance to UAE is not stated in the article; no UAE site was hit.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-21", "risk_id": "ER-02", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "Debris from a drone intercepted by Saudi air defences struck near a processing plant at Aramco''s Shaybah oilfield on 21 Oct. The Saudi Ministry of Energy said the drone was aimed at the plant; debris set a contractor vehicle on fire outside the perimeter, killing two and injuring two. The ministry said operations were not affected. No claim of responsibility was reported.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/10/21/saudi-aramco-shaybah-houthi-strike/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0021', '{"area": "Reputation", "at": "2026-10-24T04:40:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-24", "check": "Ask IT security and Finance whether payment and instruction approvals require call-back verification that a cloned voice or video could not pass.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-24", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Communications and strategy", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (10 Oct). Kept at 14 days old as no UAE deepfake signal is in the list. Article has no figures and names no utility or business cases.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-10", "risk_id": "ER-11", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "A Dubai Police Future Foresight Centre study warns AI-made fake videos and voices are getting harder to detect, threatening digital evidence and decision-making, and enabling impersonation, identity theft and fraud. It calls for awareness, verification skills and institutional preparedness. Part of the Ministry of Interior awareness campaign.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/uae/2026/10/10/dubai-police-says-deepfakes-getting-harder-to-detect/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0022', '{"area": "HSE", "at": "2026-10-25T04:38:04.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-25", "check": "Ask water production and EWEC whether any seawater intakes for desalination or power plants are near the spill path, and whether intake monitoring or booms are in place.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-25", "decision": "Watch", "func": "HSE", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Arab News (Reuters, 24 Oct) and Euronews (23 Oct); both confirm the spill and closures. The tanker attribution is from a private firm, not officials. Neither page mentions desalination or power plant intakes; any effect on water supply is unverified. No register risk covers water security, so left as Watch.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-24", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "A tanker oil spill reached the UAE coast. The Ministry of Climate Change and Environment leads containment and closed all Umm Al-Quwain beaches; Ras Al-Khaimah closed all its beaches until further notice and Sharjah closed Al-Hamriyah Beach. Authorities have not named the tanker; Orbital Risk Intelligence attributes it to the Gem No.2, hit by a projectile on 9 Oct about 13 nm off the UAE coast.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.arabnews.com/middle-east/uaes-ras-al-khaimah-shuts-beaches-amid-tanker-oil-spill-3008025"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0023', '{"area": "Cyber", "at": "2026-10-25T04:38:04.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-25", "check": "Ask OT security whether MicroSCADA X SYS600 or RTU500 units are in the network, read the advisories for affected versions and severity, and confirm patch or mitigation plans.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-25", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "IT and OT security", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the CISA bulletin of 20 Oct. Did not open the individual advisories, so severity, affected versions and exploitation status are unverified. Whether these products are installed is unknown.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-20", "risk_id": "ER-03", "source": "CISA: ICS advisories", "summary": "CISA released six ICS advisories on 20 Oct, including ICSA-26-293-04 (Hitachi Energy MicroSCADA X SYS600), ICSA-26-293-05 (Hitachi Energy RTU500) and an update to ICSA-26-062-03 (Hitachi Energy RTU500, Update A). Others cover HMS Networks/PEAK-System, WAGO and Moxa.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://content.govdelivery.com/accounts/USDHSCISA/bulletins/42fd2a7"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0024', '{"area": "Legal and regulatory", "at": "2026-10-25T04:38:04.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-25", "check": "Get the OFAC SDN list update of 21 Oct and screen shipping agents, freight forwarders and logistics suppliers used for imported network equipment.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-25", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Legal, regulatory and compliance", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the FinCEN (US Treasury) release of 21 Oct. The page does not name the UAE-based agents or give counts; the OFAC list itself was not opened.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-21", "risk_id": "ER-05", "source": "US Treasury (OFAC): press releases", "summary": "Under ''Operation Economic Outcast'', Treasury on 21 Oct sanctioned Karnakis and Karnakis, a Panama- and Greece-based law firm, and Singapore- and UAE-based shipping agents it says aid Iran''s shadow fleet. FinCEN issued its first administrative subpoena under 31 U.S.C. 5318(k) in a probe of a Greek bank, and sent banks requests on ties to designated Iranian institutions.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.fincen.gov/news/news-releases/operation-economic-outcast-targets-irans-shadow-fleet-networks"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0025', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-25T04:38:04.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-25", "check": "Check UKMTO and JMIC advisories for any confirmed mine strikes or mine warnings in the southern corridor, and ask Procurement about shipments due via Gulf ports.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Low", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-25", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Middle East Eye live blog (24 Oct). All claims come from IRGC, IRNA or Fars; no maritime authority or owner confirmation found. Use of mines would be a new tactic if confirmed. Related to ER-01 but not linked until confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-24", "risk_id": "", "source": "Middle East Eye", "summary": "The IRGC navy claimed, via IRNA on 23 Oct, that two supertankers using what it calls an ''unauthorised'' southern corridor of the Strait of Hormuz struck naval mines, with explosions and fires disabling both engine rooms. Fars cited an IRGC source claiming three more tankers were struck that Thursday. No vessel names or independent confirmation were given.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.middleeasteye.net/live-blog/live-blog-update/two-supertankers-using-unauthorised-hormuz-route-hit-naval-mines-irgc"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0026', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-25T04:38:04.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-25", "check": "Confirm the Aramco evacuation from a second reputable source, and check the current US travel advisory for the UAE, since reports differ on whether embassy families were told to leave the UAE.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-25", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Gulf News live page (updated 23 Oct) and Anadolu (21-22 Oct). Anadolu quotes the State Department spokesman that the ordered departure covers Saudi Arabia only; Gulf News also says families were told to leave the UAE, Jordan, Qatar and Bahrain, which conflicts. Aramco evacuation rests on unnamed AFP sources. Fits ER-02 if confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-23", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "AFP sources say essential staff at Aramco''s eastern headquarters were told on 22 Oct to work from home until further notice, after a Houthi strike on the Dhahran facility the week before. Dammam''s King Fahd airport was attacked on 21 Oct (two dead, eight injured). The US State Department ordered non-emergency staff and families to leave Saudi Arabia only.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/world/mena/middle-east-war-saudi-airport-attack-kills-one-as-us-orders-embassy-departures-1.500719174"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0027', '{"area": "Strategy and projects", "at": "2026-10-26T04:38:37.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-26", "check": "Confirm with the projects team the tender status, the new bid date and whether the design-build-operate model replaces the 2024 EPC tender.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-26", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Projects and construction", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the MEED guest page (20 Oct). Facts are attributed to MEED''s unnamed sources; bidders and the link to the earlier tender are not stated. No clear fit in the register; ER-09 (tender pressure) is a loose fit only.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-20", "risk_id": "", "source": "MEED: GCC projects and contracts", "summary": "MEED says Abu Dhabi''s transmission and distribution companies issued an RFP for the Mirfa-Liwa water scheme: a 128 MIGD Mirfa pumping station, about 125 km of pipelines to Muzairah with branches to Madinat Zayed and Liwa, storage tanks and four distribution clusters. Originally estimated at USD 775m. Bids now due 5 Jan 2027 (was 11 Nov); the model reportedly moves from EPC to design, build and operate.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://guest.meed.com/taqa-moves-forward-with-mirfa-liwa-scheme/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0028', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-26T04:38:37.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-26", "check": "Watch for official US or UAE statements; review readiness of control centres and critical substations, desalination interfaces and emergency staffing for a renewed escalation.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-26", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the Gulf News live page (updated 25 Oct 08:42). Strike preparations rest on WSJ and AFP reporting relayed by Gulf News; not confirmed by an official source. Fits ER-02 if escalation is confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-25", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "Gulf News (updated 25 Oct) cites the WSJ that USS George Washington in the Arabian Sea is being rearmed with standoff land-attack missiles and bunker-busters, and AFP on signs of possible renewed large-scale US strikes on Iran, incl. a planned USS Theodore Roosevelt deployment. US envoy Tom Barrack said a strike could come ''this weekend''; Trump earlier indicated no action before 3 Nov.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/world/mena/middle-east-war-houthi-missile-targets-riyadh-tankers-hit-mines-near-hormuz-1.500721804"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0029', '{"area": "Cyber", "at": "2026-10-26T04:38:37.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-26", "check": "Ask IT/OT and telecoms which SCADA, metering and corporate links depend on subsea routes through Hormuz, and confirm backup paths (terrestrial fibre, satellite).", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-26", "decision": "Watch", "func": "IT and OT security", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Oman Observer (DPA, 21 Oct) and Gulf News (24 Oct). The Reuters report itself was not opened. Cables are not named. Al Jazeera (13 Oct) also reports an Iranian warning that Gulf cables, data centres and AI facilities could be attacked. Could fit ER-03 or ER-02 after review.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-21", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "IRGC general Yadollah Javani told Al-Alam on 21 Oct that if the US damages Iran''s infrastructure, Iran could hit the ''seven major cables'' under the Strait of Hormuz to inflict serious damage on the US and its regional allies. On 24 Oct Gulf News reported two Iranian security officials told Reuters Tehran has drawn up plans to target undersea internet cables in the Gulf if fresh US and Israeli attacks occur.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.omanobserver.om/article/1198163/world/region/iran-threatens-to-attack-undersea-internet-cables-in-strait-of-hormuz"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0030', '{"area": "Strategy and projects", "at": "2026-10-26T04:38:37.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-26", "check": "Compare current Abu Dhabi distribution load forecasts with the AI campus connection plans and test a higher-demand scenario.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-26", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Network planning and engineering", "horizon": "Long", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (22 Oct, updated 23 Oct). The survey reflects industry expectations, not verified forecasts, as the article says. No UAE grid load data in the article.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-22", "risk_id": "ER-08", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "The Adipec Global Energy Report 2026 (Kekst CNC, 1,832 energy decision-makers in 78 countries) found 81% expect AI to push electricity demand above existing projections, 32% significantly higher; about a quarter say the industry is unprepared, citing grid delays. The article notes Abu Dhabi''s planned 5 GW AI campus housing Stargate UAE.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2026/10/22/ai-power-demand-underestimated-in-current-forecasts-81-of-energy-executives-say/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0031', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-27T04:38:22.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-27", "check": "Check UKMTO/JMIC advisories directly and ask key suppliers whether inbound cargo for transformers, cables and meters is among vessels waiting outside Hormuz.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-27", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the gCaptain article (26 Oct); Seatrade (26 Oct) also reports the 23 Oct late UKMTO report. UKMTO and JMIC primary pages not opened. Vessel identity not disclosed. Distinct from SQ-0018 (October record) and SQ-0025 (mines).", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-26", "risk_id": "ER-01", "source": "gCaptain: shipping and Hormuz reporting", "summary": "UKMTO received a late, verified report that an outbound tanker was disabled by an unknown projectile in the Strait of Hormuz on 23 Oct (crew safe). JMIC (25 Oct) keeps Hormuz at SEVERE with further attacks highly likely; 101 US-facilitated transits on 22-24 Oct versus about 138 a day in 2025; about 492 vessels waiting outside the Strait.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gcaptain.com/tanker-disabled-in-strait-of-hormuz-attack-another-vessel-reported-on-fire-in-persian-gulf/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0032', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-27T04:38:22.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-27", "check": "Watch for any formal Iranian transit rules, fees or routing requirements for Hormuz and assess the effect on lead times and costs for imported network equipment.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-27", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The Korea Times (AFP, 25 Oct) and Mehr News (same quotes, undated). Gulf News live blog (26 Oct) adds that Iran''s armed forces chief said the strait is closed to vessels not following Iranian rules; that line is from a grade C source and not used in the summary. No concrete new rules published yet.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-25", "risk_id": "ER-01", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "Iran''s Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi said at a televised event in Tehran on 25 Oct that shipping routes through the Strait of Hormuz and the management of the strait ''will no longer be the same'', and called for the complete absence of foreign forces in the region. The US maintains a naval counter-blockade on Iranian ports.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/world/20261025/iran-says-resumption-of-war-would-not-change-its-stances"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0033', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-27T04:38:22.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-27", "check": "Look for Saudi Ministry of Energy or Aramco confirmation of damage, and note any similar targeting of UAE bypass routes such as Fujairah.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-27", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Communications and strategy", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The Star (Reuters wire, 26 Oct). The attack itself is a Houthi claim and unverified; the page confirms only that the claim was made. Distinct from SQ-0020 (Shaybah) and SQ-0026 (Dhahran).", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-26", "risk_id": "ER-02", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "The Houthis claimed attacks on Saudi Arabia''s East-West crude pipeline pumping stations on 26 Oct, after a Saturday claim also naming an Aramco facility in Yanbu and the Rabigh refinery. There was no immediate Saudi confirmation and no damage reported. Reuters notes the pipeline is a key export route while Hormuz is largely shut.", "touches": "No", "url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/news/world/2026/10/26/houthis-say-they-attacked-saudi-oil-pumping-stations-riyadh-airport-as-fighting-intensifies"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0034', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-28T04:41:17.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-28", "check": "Ask the bulk water supplier whether any Abu Dhabi desalination intakes are on alert or derated, and whether MOCCAE has issued guidance on the slick''s drift; review water storage and supply contingency.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-28", "decision": "New risk", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Naharnet (AFP, 27 Oct) and The New Arab (AFP, 28 Oct); CBS News live updates (27 Oct, AFP) carry the same facts. Effect on the Naqaa plant and on any Abu Dhabi plant is unverified; no official statement on intakes was found. Update to SQ-0022. No register risk covers water supply contamination, so a new risk on desalination intake disruption is proposed for review.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-27", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "AFP satellite analysis shows the tanker oil slick off the UAE grew from about 180 sq km on 21 Oct to about 750 sq km three days later. Imagery from 26 Oct showed slicks a few hundred metres from the intake of the Naqaa desalination plant; PAX said it is unclear how far plant operation will be affected. Oil reached Umm Al Quwain beaches, which were closed; clean-up is ongoing.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.naharnet.com/stories/en/323381-experts-warn-of-effects-of-slick-as-oil-seen-on-uae-beach"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0035', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-28T04:41:17.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-28", "check": "Look for Saudi Ministry of Energy or Aramco confirmation of any damage, and for any statement on threats to UAE energy sites.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Low", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-28", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Communications and strategy", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Anadolu Agency (27 Oct); CBS News live updates (AFP, 27 Oct) report the same claim and give refinery capacity as 550,000 b/d. Reuters also carried it (US News, Investing.com) but those pages were not opened. The strike and damage are a Houthi claim only. Distinct from SQ-0033 (East-West pipeline claim). Possible fit ER-02 once confirmed. Anadolu is not in the sources list; filed under news wires.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-27", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "The Houthis said on 27 Oct they fired a ballistic missile at Saudi Arabia''s Ras Tanura refinery in the Eastern Province and claimed it caused large fires. Saudi authorities made no immediate comment. The Saudi-led coalition said it intercepted four drones and three ballistic missiles launched toward the kingdom earlier that day.", "touches": "No", "url": "https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/yemen-s-houthis-claim-missile-attack-on-saudi-arabia-s-ras-tanura-oil-refinery/4102578"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0036', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-28T04:41:17.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-28", "check": "Check UKMTO and JMIC for confirmation of a mine strike on 27 Oct and any change in threat level; ask freight forwarders about effects on inbound equipment shipments.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Low", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-28", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Gulf News (updated 28 Oct, grade C) and Anadolu Agency (27 Oct), which reports the Iranian Navy statement via IRNA with no vessel named and no independent confirmation. No UKMTO report of this incident was found. Follows the similar claim in SQ-0025. Possible fit ER-01 once confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-28", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "Iran''s army said an oil tanker hit mines and caught fire after using a route Tehran had not authorised east of Hormuz; Iran''s chief of staff said the strait is ''completely closed'' to ships that do not comply. CENTCOM said its forces remain present in the strait. The UK issued fresh alerts covering the UAE and 14 other countries, saying the risk of sudden escalation remains high.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/uae/us-israel-iran-war-what-uae-residents-need-to-know-today-oct-28-2026-1.500726331"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0037', '{"area": "HSE", "at": "2026-10-28T04:41:17.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-28", "check": "Check NCM alerts for Al Ain and the Western Region, and review fault logs for rain or dust related outages and late-season peak load.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-28", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (27 Oct). Also opened Gulf Business (19 Oct), which reports the NCM Seasonal Climate Outlook for Oct to Dec 2026: warmer than average with over 80% probability, 0.5 to 1.5 C above normal, near to above normal rain; NCM page itself not opened. Continues SQ-0010 and SQ-0016. Context for ER-10; no utility impact reported.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-27", "risk_id": "", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "Hail and heavy rain hit Ras Al Khaimah and Fujairah on 27 Oct. The NCM issued a high-wind alert (up to 45 km/h, dust, low visibility) for northern, eastern and southern areas and forecasts heavy rain in Al Ain until Thursday. Daytime highs stay in the mid to high 30s C in Abu Dhabi, reaching 40 C in Al Ain and remote areas; the article links the delayed cooling to El Nino. No power impact reported.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/uae/2026/10/27/hail-hits-northern-emirates-as-uae-weather-alert-issued-over-45kph-winds/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0038', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-28T04:41:17.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-28", "check": "Check the LME official price and ask cable and transformer suppliers whether copper-linked price adjustments apply to open orders.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-28", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened MINING.COM (Reuters, 27 Oct). Not checked against LME data. Reverses the fall in SQ-0017 (22 Oct low). ER-07 (critical minerals) is Closed, so no risk link.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-27", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "LME three-month copper rose 1.1% to USD 14,487.50/t on 27 Oct, its strongest since 16 Oct. The cash contract traded at a USD 199.50/t premium to three-month, near its widest since 27 Aug, and the Yangshan premium reached USD 188/t, a near 13-year high. Drivers cited: rebounding AI stocks, tight concentrate supply and strong Chinese demand.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.mining.com/web/copper-price-climbs-on-ai-rebound-china-demand-strength/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0039', '{"area": "Finance", "at": "2026-10-29T04:45:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-29", "check": "Confirm on the CBUAE website and check what the hold means for floating-rate debt and planned project financing.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-29", "decision": "Add to existing risk", "func": "Finance and treasury", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Zawya (WAM byline, 29 Oct) and Emirates 24|7 (28 Oct), which agree. Effective date and Fed rate level not stated on either page. Follows the 25 bp rise in SQ-0009; rates now on hold.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-29", "risk_id": "ER-06", "source": "WAM (Emirates News Agency): energy, cyber and government", "summary": "The CBUAE kept the Base Rate on the Overnight Deposit Facility unchanged at 3.9%, after the US Federal Reserve kept the Interest Rate on Reserve Balances unchanged on 28 Oct. Standing credit facilities stay at 50 basis points above the Base Rate.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://www.zawya.com/en/economy/cbuae-maintains-base-rate-at-3.9-1855073"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0040', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-29T04:45:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-29", "check": "Watch for a US response and for UKMTO/JMIC transit data after 3 Nov; check whether supplier shipping lead times change.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-29", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The Star (AFP, 29 Oct). Gulf News live page (updated 29 Oct) carries the same plan and conditions. Straits.live brief of 28 Oct says IMF PortWatch logged 4 transits on 18 Oct vs 85 a day pre-crisis. Not confirmed by a grade A source. Relates to ER-01; different event from SQ-0032.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-29", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "Iran''s Foreign Minister said on 28 Oct that Tehran is discussing with mediators how to carry out its seven-day plan to end the war and reopen the Strait of Hormuz. Conditions include a region-wide ceasefire, unfrozen assets, lifted oil sanctions and an end to the US naval blockade. Axios reports Qatar-led mediators seek to restart US-Iran talks and prevent war resuming after the 3 Nov US midterms.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thestar.com.my/news/world/2026/10/29/iran-says-discussing-plan-with-mediators-to-end-war-reopen-hormuz"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0041', '{"area": "Cyber", "at": "2026-10-29T04:45:00.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-29", "check": "Check whether RUGGEDCOM CROSSBOW is used for substation remote access, and confirm affected and fixed versions in Siemens ProductCERT and CISA ICSA-26-295-12.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-29", "decision": "Watch", "func": "IT and OT security", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened ISSSource (27 Oct). The page lists versions up to 6.0 as affected and V6.0 as the fix, which conflicts; confirm in vendor advisory. CISA page ICSA-26-295-12 found in search but could not be opened. Relates to ER-03.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-27", "risk_id": "", "source": "ISSSource", "summary": "Siemens and CISA disclosed 11 vulnerabilities in RUGGEDCOM CROSSBOW, a secure access management product for critical infrastructure: several SQL injections (CVSS v3 up to 8.8), exposure of admin credentials in config data, and missing authorisation checks, including access to substation and device data. Most need an authenticated attacker. No exploitation reported. Update to V6.0 or later is advised.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://isssource.com/siemens-clears-ruggedcom-crossbow-issues"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0042', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-30T04:38:38.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-30", "check": "Open UKMTO Warning 185-26 (29 Oct) and JMIC advisories to confirm details; check with freight forwarders whether inbound transformer, cable and meter shipments are delayed or rerouted.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-30", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Arab News (Reuters story, 30 Oct). Dhow and mine claims from Gulf News live blog (updated 29 Oct, https://gulfnews.com/world/mena/middle-east-war-saudi-intercepts-houthi-missile-as-iran-warns-israel-against-strikes-1.500727751) and Anadolu (https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/fire-reported-on-vessel-in-strait-of-hormuz-ukmto/4104568). UKMTO PDF found in search but could not be opened. Iranian mine claims are not independently confirmed; flags and timing unknown. Relates to ER-01.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-30", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "UKMTO said a small boat attached two explosive devices to an outbound tanker''s hull about 25 nm NE of Khasab, Oman, on 29 Oct; an engine-room fire temporarily disabled it, crew safe, no pollution, and it continued its voyage. The same day UKMTO reported a dhow fire 9 nm N of Khasab (it sank, crew evacuated), and Iran claimed at least four tankers caught fire after hitting mines.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.arabnews.com/middle-east/fire-hit-tanker-continues-journey-after-being-attacked-in-strait-of-hormuz-ukmto-says-3008930"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0043', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-30T04:38:38.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-30", "check": "Confirm through official UAE statements or NCEMA/ADCMC guidance whether readiness measures are requested; review emergency and continuity plans for loss of generation or gas supply in early November.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-30", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened WNDU (AP story, 28 Oct EDT / 29 Oct UTC) and RTE (PA, 29 Oct, https://www.rte.ie/news/2026/1029/1597154-us-iran-strikes/). Also in Gulf News live blog. Based on anonymous diplomats; White House declined comment. Allies receiving the warning are not named. Relates to ER-02.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-29", "risk_id": "", "source": "Associated Press (AP) (via republishing sites)", "summary": "AP, citing two anonymous diplomats, reports US officials told several Middle East allies to prepare for possible renewed US strikes on Iran after the 3 Nov midterms, lasting several days, and for Iranian retaliation; allies were urged to take precautions against strikes on energy facilities and other critical infrastructure. Trump has not decided. The UAE urged political solutions.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.wndu.com/2026/10/29/us-warns-allies-prepare-possible-iran-strikes-retaliation-after-elections-ap-sources-say/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0044', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-30T04:38:38.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-30", "check": "Ask the water supply planner whether any desalination source feeding the network (e.g. Taweelah) is in the slick''s drift path, and confirm MOCCAE or EWEC statements on intake monitoring.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-30", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened WTAQ (Reuters explainer, 29 Oct) and Baird Maritime (same Reuters story, https://www.bairdmaritime.com/security/emergency-services/pollution-control/feature-uae-grapples-with-coastal-oil-spill-as-water-supply-risks-emerge). Follows spill signals SQ-0029 and SQ-0033; new angle is the desalination intake threat. Tanker identity is from shipping sources, not confirmed by authorities. No register risk covers water supply contamination.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-29", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "Reuters reports verified footage showing the tanker oil slick about 2 km from the Naqa''a desalination plant (Umm Al Quwain/Ras Al Khaimah border); Windward said it threatened the plant''s seawater intake. No UAE plant shutdowns announced. Sharjah closed all beaches. Desalination supplies over 80% of UAE potable water; experts say intakes are the main vulnerability and plants should shut if oil nears.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://wtaq.com/2026/10/29/explainer-how-could-the-oil-spill-off-the-uae-coast-affect-desalination-plants/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0045', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-10-31T04:38:10.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-31", "check": "Confirm on UKMTO and JMIC how many vessels were hit on 30 Oct and whether war-risk rates or transits for cargo bound for Abu Dhabi ports have changed; ask Procurement about inbound shipments of transformers, cables and meters.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-31", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened ThePrint (Reuters, Dubai, 30 Oct) and Gulf News live page (updated 30 Oct; AP could not verify mine claims; US denied mine claims; Oman evacuated 25 crew from a Panama-flagged vessel on fire off Musandam). IRGC claims are unverified; unclear whether the UKMTO vessels are among the four. Follows SQ-0042 (29 Oct limpet attack). Fits ER-01 if confirmed. Also seen: https://gulfnews.com/world/mena/middle-east-war-iran-claims-tankers-hit-mines-in-strait-of-hormuz-ukmto-confirms-strike-off-oman-fired-us-general-reportedly-admitted-iran-leaks-1.500729137", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-30", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "Reuters (30 Oct): the IRGC Navy said four oil tankers caught fire and exploded in the Strait of Hormuz while using ''unauthorised routes'', two carrying about 2 million barrels each; Reuters could not verify. UKMTO separately reported a vessel hit by an unknown projectile about 40 nm south of Lavan Island (fire, crew safe) and a crude tanker struck on outbound transit.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://theprint.in/world/irans-irgc-navy-says-four-tankers-catch-fire-in-strait-of-hormuz/3086698/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0046', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-10-31T04:38:10.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-31", "check": "Confirm with the water supply planner that no desalination source feeding the organisation''s network was affected and whether intake monitoring continues; watch for any renewed leak during salvage of the tanker.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-31", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (30 Oct) and a Reuters report republished by WMBD Radio (30 Oct, https://www.wmbdradio.com/2026/10/30/uae-says-oil-leak-from-tanker-has-been-stopped-pollution-eases/), both citing the Environment Ministry via WAM. Two independent grade B sources agree on the facts written. Follow-up to SQ-0034 and SQ-0044 (easing, not escalation). The National names the Union Water and Electricity Company (northern emirates utility) as monitoring intakes; no Abu Dhabi plant is named. Cause of damage not stated by authorities; Reuters shipping sources say a projectile hit on 9 Oct. No register risk covers water supply contamination.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-30", "risk_id": "", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "UAE authorities said on 30 Oct the oil leak from tanker Gem No. 2 was stopped and the spill contained, with no new leakage. The slick is concentrated off Umm Al Quwain, partly towards Ras Al Khaimah, Ajman and Sharjah; pollution density has fallen. Some beaches remain closed. Officials say precautions to protect drinking water will not affect supply, and seawater at intake points is being monitored.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/uae/2026/10/30/uae-tanker-gem-no-2-oil-spill-contained/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0047', '{"area": "Cyber", "at": "2026-10-31T04:38:10.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-10-31", "check": "Ask Asset management whether CoreTec4 or CoreTec5 units are installed on the organisation''s transformers; if so, confirm versions, network exposure and upgrade plan with OT security.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-10-31", "decision": "Watch", "func": "IT and OT security", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. The CISA page could not be opened directly (site error); facts read from the GCVE mirror of ICSA-26-302-03 (https://db.gcve.eu/vuln/icsa-26-302-03) and OpenCVE for CVE-2026-13162 (https://app.opencve.io/cve/CVE-2026-13162). Confirm on CISA or Hitachi Energy PSIRT before relying on it. A vulnerability, not a campaign, so not linked to ER-03.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-29", "risk_id": "", "source": "CISA: ICS advisories", "summary": "CISA advisory ICSA-26-302-03 (first published 27 Oct, updated 29 Oct): Hitachi Energy CoreTec4 and CoreTec5 transformer monitoring devices, versions 3.4.0 and earlier, have an OS command injection flaw (CVE-2026-13162, CVSS 3.1 7.5) and a local root privilege escalation in the Linux kernel (CVE-2026-43284, CVSS 8.8). Fix: CoreTec5 version 5.0.0. Energy sector, deployed worldwide.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.cisa.gov/news-events/ics-advisories/icsa-26-302-03"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0048', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-11-01T04:38:47.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-01", "check": "Ask Procurement and supply chain whether any inbound equipment, fuel or chemical shipments for the organisation transit Hormuz in November, and confirm with the gas supplier whether LNG or gas deliveries to power and water plants are affected.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-01", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (31 Oct, UKMTO counts and the 30 Oct outbound tanker strike), ANI (31 Oct, https://aninews.in/news/world/asia/entire-crew-including-six-indian-seafarers-safe-after-marshall-islands-flagged-lng-carrier-struck-in-persian-gulf-sonowal20261031191837/, Al Mayeda, Marshall Islands flag) and Anadolu (31 Oct, https://www.aa.com.tr/en/middle-east/tanker-struck-by-unidentified-projectile-in-strait-of-hormuz-uk-maritime-agency/4107027). Gulf News live blog (1 Nov) also reports Al Mayeda and a UKMTO warning of a fishing vessel boarded on 30 Oct. Damage to Al Mayeda and its cargo owner not stated. UKMTO page not opened; monthly count is a single grade B source, so not linked. Fits ER-01 if confirmed; follows SQ-0045 and SQ-0018.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-10-31", "risk_id": "", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "UKMTO recorded more than 30 incidents in and around Hormuz, the Gulf of Oman and the Arabian Gulf in October, the highest monthly total of the war and over double September; 145 since the war began, and the real number may be higher. A crude tanker was struck leaving the strait on 30 Oct. India''s shipping minister said LNG carrier Al Mayeda was hit by a projectile in the Gulf on 30 Oct; all 25 crew safe.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/10/31/attacks-on-ships-transiting-hormuz-in-october-highest-since-start-of-war/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0049', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-11-02T04:38:55.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-02", "check": "Confirm the statement on WAM or an official UAE channel, and ask Network operations and control whether emergency and continuity plans for renewed attacks on power and water sites are current.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-02", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (1 Nov) and the AP report republished by ABC News (1 Nov, https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/united-arab-emirates-military-solutions-offer-quick-off-137752713), which also cites IISS that the UAE faced more than 3,000 drone and missile strikes before the April ceasefire. Gulf News evening brief (1 Nov) carries the same remarks. No official UAE transcript opened; one grade B and one grade C source, so not linked. Fits ER-02 and ER-01 if confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-01", "risk_id": "", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "Speaking at the IISS Manama Dialogue on 1 Nov, UAE presidential diplomatic adviser Dr Anwar Gargash said the UAE does not want another round of confrontation but is ''braced for the worst'' if US and Iranian positions are not bridged. He called restoring the pre-war situation in Hormuz a non-negotiable Gulf priority and said the GCC has not collectively risen to the challenge.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/gulf/2026/11/01/uae-does-not-want-new-round-of-conflict-but-is-braced-for-worst-says-dr-gargash/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0050', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-11-02T04:38:55.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-02", "check": "Check UKMTO and JMIC for any report matching the IRGC claim, and ask Procurement and supply chain whether any of the organisation''s inbound shipments are routed through Hormuz this month.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Low", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-02", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the Reuters dispatch on Internazionale (partly paywalled, machine-translated). The National live blog (2 Nov, https://www.thenationalnews.com/news/mena/2026/11/02/live-iran-war-oil-prices-trump/) also carries the IRGC claim, Saudi condemnation of an attack on a Qatari LNG carrier, and oil prices falling more than 3% as Trump signals more time for diplomacy (no price levels given). Straits.live brief (1 Nov) reports a Saba-only claim of a tanker fire east of the strait. Claim is single-sided and unverified; continues SQ-0045 and SQ-0048. Fits ER-01 if confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-01", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "Reuters (1 Nov), citing Iranian state media: the IRGC Navy said two oil tankers ''exploded'' after hitting mines while using an ''unauthorised route'' in the Strait of Hormuz. No ship names, flags, cargo or crew details were given and no independent confirmation was cited.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.internazionale.it/ultime-notizie-reuters/2026/11/01/iran-s-irgc-navy-says-two-tankers-exploded-after-hitting-mines-in-hormuz"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0051', '{"area": "Finance", "at": "2026-11-02T04:38:55.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-02", "check": "Confirm the November prices from the UAE Fuel Price Committee or Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure announcement, and update fleet and standby-generator fuel cost assumptions.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-02", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Finance and treasury", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the Gulf News 1 Nov brief (last updated 11:54, 1 Nov). Official fuel price committee release not opened; Gulf News is grade C, so unverified. Relevant to ER-04 (diesel and refined-product tightness).", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-01", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "UAE retail fuel prices for November (effective 1 Nov): diesel AED 4.75 per litre, down from AED 4.80 in October; Super 98 AED 4.16, Special 95 AED 4.04 and E-Plus 91 AED 3.97, each down AED 0.24.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/world/mena/us-iran-israel-tensions-rise-what-uae-residents-need-to-know-on-november-1-1.500731511"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0052', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-11-03T04:38:30.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-03", "check": "Confirm both incidents and the JMIC figures on the UKMTO and JMIC pages, and ask logistics whether any inbound transformer, cable or meter shipments are among the waiting vessels.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-03", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened gCaptain (2 Nov, Mike Schuler) and Asharq Al-Awsat (1 Nov, https://english.aawsat.com/world/5336401-ukmto-vessel-struck-strait-hormuz), which confirms the 1 Nov Hormuz strike via UKMTO. Khaleej Times live blog (2 Nov) also lists a further UKMTO report of a vessel hit by a projectile off Oman late on 2 Nov, not verified. UKMTO and JMIC pages not opened; single grade B source for the JMIC figures. Fits ER-01 if confirmed; follows SQ-0048.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-02", "risk_id": "", "source": "gCaptain: shipping and Hormuz reporting", "summary": "UKMTO reported a tanker hit by two projectiles about 72 nm east of Ras Al Khafji, Saudi Arabia, at 2347 UTC on 1 Nov (crew safe), and a merchant vessel hit by an unknown projectile in Hormuz at 1509 UTC (Warning 191-26). JMIC (1 Nov) rated the Hormuz threat SEVERE: 18 confirmed attacks since 6 Oct and about 490 vessels waiting outside the strait.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://gcaptain.com/new-wave-of-attacks-hits-tankers-and-lng-carrier-in-strait-of-hormuz-and-persian-gulf/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0053', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-11-03T04:38:30.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-03", "check": "Check with the regulator and EWEC whether the resilience redesign the minister described will extend to power, water and network assets, and whether new hardening requirements are expected.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-03", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the Reuters story republished on gCaptain (Abu Dhabi dateline, 2 Nov). Khaleej Times live blog (2 Nov, grade C) carries the same two remarks. The article gives no details on power or water assets; impact on the organisation is unverified. Related to ER-02 (attacks on Gulf energy sites); follows SQ-0050 (Gargash remarks).", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-02", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "Reuters (2 Nov): UAE Energy Minister Suhail al-Mazrouei told reporters at ADIPEC in Abu Dhabi that the UAE will protect its energy infrastructure and invest in new export routes, storage abroad and shipping fleets. He said the course of the war with Iran cannot be predicted but the UAE will be better prepared, and companies will need to redesign facilities for resilience. A new pipeline to Fujairah will double crude capacity by next year.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gcaptain.com/uae-to-protect-energy-infrastructure-invest-in-new-export-routes-to-prepare-for-iran-war-minister-says/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0054', '{"area": "Strategy and projects", "at": "2026-11-03T04:38:30.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-03", "check": "Confirm the figures in a WAM or Ministry of Energy and Infrastructure release, and find out how much of the network spend falls in Abu Dhabi and on distribution.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-03", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network planning and engineering", "horizon": "Long", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Gulf News (last updated 23:00, 2 Nov); headline says Dh200 billion, body says Dh150 to 200 billion. No WAM or ministry release found; single grade C source, so unverified. No split by emirate or by transmission and distribution given. Relevant to ER-08 (Abu Dhabi power demand doubling by 2050).", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-02", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "At an ADIPEC 2026 ministerial panel, UAE Energy Minister Suhail Al Mazrouei said the UAE plans Dh150 to 200 billion of energy investment by 2030 in generation capacity, electricity networks, storage and integrated system operations, citing demand from advanced industries, AI and data centres. Clean energy was 32.4% of UAE electricity generation in 2025, against a 35% target for 2031.", "touches": "Yes", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/business/energy/uae-plans-dh200-billion-energy-investment-by-2030-suhail-al-mazrouei-1.500733116"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0055', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-11-04T04:39:42.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-04", "check": "Watch for Iranian retaliation against Gulf states or energy and water sites, and for NCEMA or ADCMC guidance; confirm emergency and continuity plans for loss of generation or gas supply are current.", "checked": "Yes", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-04", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (3 Nov, updated 09:12) and the Reuters story republished by KFGO (3 Nov, https://kfgo.com/2026/11/02/oil-rises-after-report-of-us-strike-on-irans-qeshm-island/); both report the strike via US officials and the price moves. Al Jazeera (3 Nov) and the Gulf News live page (3 Nov, grade C) add IRGC claims of downed US drones, which CENTCOM called false. No official US statement opened. No attack on a UAE site reported; escalation context for ER-02 rather than evidence. Follows SQ-0043 (US warning to allies).", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-03", "risk_id": "", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "US forces struck Iran''s Qeshm Island, at the mouth of Hormuz, on the night of 2 Nov; US officials called the strikes defensive, aimed at stopping attacks on commercial shipping. Iranian state media reported several explosions. Brent fell over 7% on 2 Nov to about $104.8 on deal hopes, then rose to about $107 on 3 Nov as the strikes revived supply fears.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2026/11/03/oil-prices-cross-105-after-us-strikes-on-irans-qeshm-island/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0056', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-11-04T04:39:42.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-04", "check": "Confirm the incident on the UKMTO site and check whether JMIC threat levels or war-risk rates changed; ask Procurement whether inbound transformer, cable or meter shipments are delayed.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-04", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Arab News (AFP, 3 Nov). The article calls the vessel a cargo vessel in its bullets and a tanker in its text; Fox News live page (3 Nov) calls it a dhow and cites UKMTO. CBS News live page (3 Nov) also reports it. UKMTO page not opened. Crew member''s name left out. Follows SQ-0052. Fits ER-01 if confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-03", "risk_id": "", "source": "News wires: Reuters, AFP, DPA (via republishing sites)", "summary": "AFP (3 Nov): the India-flagged vessel MSV Al Jusufi, with 14 Indian crew, was hit by an ''unidentified aerial object'' off Oman; one crew member died and the Omani Coast Guard rescued 13. India''s shipping minister confirmed the death. Fox News reports UKMTO logged an attack on an Indian-crewed dhow outbound through the Strait on 2 Nov.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.arabnews.com/world/indian-sailor-killed-after-vessel-attacked-off-oman-3009541"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0057', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-11-05T04:38:23.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-05", "check": "Confirm the Lima incident and current transit counts on UKMTO and JMIC pages, and ask logistics whether any inbound transformer, cable or meter shipments are among the vessels waiting outside Hormuz.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-05", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Gulf News (last updated 4 Nov 10:15), Xinhua (4 Nov, https://english.news.cn/europe/20261104/0ccb4250bf91488697fb23cf78ff09d0/c.html: UKMTO, Tuesday 3 Nov 19:00 GMT, company security officer report) and Logistics Middle East (4 Nov, https://www.logisticsmiddleeast.com/news/tanker-struck-14-nautical-miles-northeast-of-lima, which dates it 4 Nov). IRGC claim from the Reuters story on JPost (4 Nov, https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-913786), which adds two vessels seized. Transit counts are Gulf News only; Bloomberg (via Rigzone, 4 Nov) says Hormuz flows are near pre-war levels, which conflicts. UKMTO page not opened; tanker name and flag unknown. Follows SQ-0056. Fits ER-01 if confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-04", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "UKMTO reported a tanker struck by two unidentified projectiles about 14 nm northeast of Lima, Oman, hitting the engine room; no casualties or environmental damage. Gulf News says only five commodity vessels crossed Hormuz on Saturday and none on Sunday, against more than 130 a day pre-war. On 4 Nov the IRGC claimed four tankers were destroyed by mines south of the strait; not independently verified.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/uae/usisrael-iran-war-what-uae-residents-need-to-know-today-nov-4-2026-1.500735252"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0058', '{"area": "Finance", "at": "2026-11-05T04:38:23.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-05", "check": "Confirm settlement prices on ICE or a Reuters report, and ask Finance whether fuel, diesel and energy cost assumptions for fleet, standby generation and contracts should be revisited if prices hold below $100.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-05", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Finance and treasury", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Rigzone (Bloomberg, 4 Nov 3:50 PM EST) and Oilprice.com (4 Nov, staff writer, intraday Brent $100.60, Murban $100.90). Gulf News live blog (updated 5 Nov 07:33) reports Brent at $93.63 early 5 Nov Beijing time. Bloomberg is not in the sources list, so it was added for review (grade C). Prices are volatile and may reverse if fighting resumes. Possible relevance to ER-04 (diesel and refined products) and ER-06; Bloomberg''s statement that Hormuz flows are near pre-war levels conflicts with other reports.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-04", "risk_id": "", "source": "Bloomberg (via republishing sites)", "summary": "Bloomberg (4 Nov): Brent January settled 8.7% lower at $94.62, the lowest since 31 Aug, after trading as low as $93.22; WTI December fell 8.3% to $88.12. Drivers cited: the US midterm results, seen by investors as a faster route to ending the war, and Trump telling the FT he had no immediate plans to ramp up fighting. JPMorgan estimated a 1.4 million b/d oil surplus in October.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.rigzone.com/news/wire/oil_plunges_as_election_shifts_iran_outlook-04-nov-2026-185012-article/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0059', '{"area": "Operations", "at": "2026-11-05T04:38:23.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-05", "check": "Watch for official US, UAE or NCEMA/ADCMC statements; confirm emergency and continuity plans for loss of generation, gas or desalination supply are current if major combat resumes.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-05", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network operations and control", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the Gulf News live blog (newest entry 07:21, 5 Nov) and Al Jazeera (4 Nov, Anadolu and Reuters, https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/4/iran-says-us-reply-to-hormuz-plan-unconvincing-trump-confirms-strikes): Trump confirmed a ''minor'' US strike on an Iranian anti-aircraft facility early 3 Nov; Iran''s Rezaei called the US reply ''not convincing''; Iranian officials suggested Gulf undersea cables could be targeted. Gulf News 4 Nov brief and a Newsmax report on Yahoo (2 Nov) cite WSJ that some Arab states warned Iran they could retaliate if their infrastructure is hit, and that the UAE and Qatar held security drills. Oilprice.com quotes Trump telling the FT there are no immediate plans to strike. Mixed signals; Axios claim not opened directly. No attack on a UAE site reported. Fits ER-02 if escalation is confirmed; follows SQ-0055 and SQ-0043.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-05", "risk_id": "", "source": "Gulf News / Khaleej Times / TradeArabia: UAE business and utilities", "summary": "Gulf News live blog (updated 5 Nov): Trump warned of a ''heavy hit'' on Iran, saying ''We have to do something large''; US officials told Axios the military is finishing preparations for a possible resumption of major combat operations, which is not an order. Iran demands an end to the US naval blockade, sanctions relief and release of frozen funds before it reopens Hormuz. Qatari mediators are seeking backing for a draft deal.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://gulfnews.com/world/mena/middle-east-conflict-trump-warns-of-heavy-hit-as-iran-says-americans-voted-no-to-war-1.500735100"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0060', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-11-06T04:37:45.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-06", "check": "Confirm the Qatar incident on the UKMTO site and any JMIC threat or transit update; ask logistics whether inbound transformer, cable or meter shipments are delayed or rerouted.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-06", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Procurement and supply chain", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Regional", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened Al Jazeera (published 5 Nov, with AFP, AP and Reuters) and the ABC News live page (updated 5 Nov 05:02 EST), which quotes the UKMTO notice. Khaleej Times live blog (5 Nov) lists both the UKMTO report and the IRGC claim. UKMTO page not opened; vessel name and flag unknown. The Hill and a republished AP story could not be opened. Al Jazeera is not in the sources list, so it was added for review (grade C). Follows SQ-0057. Fits ER-01 if confirmed.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-05", "risk_id": "", "source": "Al Jazeera", "summary": "UKMTO reported a tanker struck by two unidentified projectiles about 50 nm north of Madinat ash Shamal, Qatar, at 23:20 GMT on 4 Nov; crew status, damage and environmental impact unconfirmed. On 5 Nov Iranian forces (IRGC via Fars, army via IRNA) claimed at least five tankers and a tugboat caught fire after hitting mines in and east of Hormuz; not independently verified.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/5/iran-says-tankers-struck-in-hormuz-amid-fears-of-new-us-attack"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0061', '{"area": "Supply chain", "at": "2026-11-06T04:37:45.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-06", "check": "Ask the bulk power and water supplier whether new gas commitments to the Northern Emirates change gas allocation or reliability for Abu Dhabi power and water plants.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "Medium", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-06", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network planning and engineering", "horizon": "Medium", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened The National (4 Nov, updated 09:15). ADNOC Gas release not opened; single grade B source. The page does not mention Abu Dhabi power or water plants or the Abu Dhabi grid, so any effect on the organisation is unverified. No register risk covers gas supply to generation; context only.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-04", "risk_id": "", "source": "The National: Abu Dhabi energy coverage", "summary": "ADNOC Gas signed a supply agreement on 4 Nov with Etihad Water and Electricity to provide natural gas for new power generation capacity in the Northern Emirates. No volumes, capacities or dates were given. ADNOC Gas says it supplies 60% of UAE sales gas needs; its Estidama project extends the gas pipeline network from 3,200 km to more than 3,500 km.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.thenationalnews.com/business/energy/2026/11/04/adnoc-gas-signs-agreement-to-supply-natural-gas-to-northern-emirates/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0062', '{"area": "Strategy and projects", "at": "2026-11-06T04:37:45.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-06", "check": "Ask Network planning whether added domestic gas from 2029 changes generation or supply assumptions in the Abu Dhabi demand and connection forecasts.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-06", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Network planning and engineering", "horizon": "Long", "level": "Local", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the ADNOC press release on Energy Connects (2 Nov) and OilPrice.com (2 Nov), which adds the 200 km location and the 90% ADNOC / 10% TotalEnergies split. WAM page (https://www.wam.ae/en/article/c31xbyf-adnoc-takes-fid-ruwais-diyab-unconventional-gas) did not load. Four days old but not in the register. Neither page names power or water plants; relevance to the organisation is indirect. Context for ER-08.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-02", "risk_id": "", "source": "ADNOC news", "summary": "ADNOC took a final investment decision on 2 Nov at ADIPEC for the Ruwais Diyab unconventional gas development, about 200 km west of Abu Dhabi: 345 mmscfd of raw gas from 2029 for 25 years, potentially up to 1 bcf/d, processed on site and linked to the UAE gas network by new pipelines. Demand drivers cited include power generation, industry and AI and data centres. Investment not stated.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.energyconnects.com/opinion/features/2026/november/adnoc-takes-fid-on-ruwais-diyab-unconventional-gas-development/"}'::jsonb),
('signals', 'SQ-0063', '{"area": "Legal and regulatory", "at": "2026-11-06T04:37:45.000Z", "by": "claude", "captured": "2026-11-06", "check": "Open the Treasury release (https://home.treasury.gov/news/press-releases/sb0681/) and the SDN list for the full names; screen shipping agents and forwarders, and check that vessels carrying the organisation''s imports are not on disavowed registries.", "checked": "Unsure", "conf": "High", "decided_by": "claude", "decided_on": "2026-11-06", "decision": "Watch", "func": "Legal, regulatory and compliance", "horizon": "Short", "level": "Global", "notes": "Proposed by the system, to confirm. Opened the US State Department statement (4 Nov). It names no UAE-based entity and no vessels; the Treasury release with the full list was not opened. Splash247 and Washington Times reports could not be opened; Khaleej Times live blog (5 Nov) also reports the action. State Department is not in the sources list, so it was added for review (grade C). Relates to ER-05; follows SQ-0024.", "proposed": true, "published": "2026-11-04", "risk_id": "", "source": "US Department of State: spokesperson press statements", "summary": "The US Treasury on 4 Nov sanctioned 13 individuals and companies in a network, led by two India-based individuals, that sold fraudulent flag registrations posing as registries of Guyana, Eswatini, Aruba, Mali, Mozambique, Malawi, Sint Maarten and Timor-Leste to Iran''s shadow fleet, plus a Turkiye-based ground-services firm for sanctioned Iranian airlines, under E.O. 13902.", "touches": "Unsure", "url": "https://www.state.gov/releases/office-of-the-spokesman/2026/11/u-s-sanctions-fraudulent-ship-registries-and-aviation-support-for-iranian-regime/"}'::jsonb),
